[00:49.06] Let me walk a while alone
[00:53.52] Among the sacred rocks and stones
[00:59.42] Let me look in vain belief
[01:04.42] Upon the beauty of each leaf
[01:21.58] There is green in every blade
[01:26.22] The tree tops lean providing shade
[01:31.90] Maypoles spin in happy sound
[01:36.86] All nature's strength around
[01:53.36] And there's a horse that feels no pain
[01:58.10] Its iron strength to take the strain
[02:04.18] Children rock it to and fro
[02:09.08] And gaily drink its colour-glow
[02:14.88] Above, the sky, devoid of cloud
[02:49.50] Thinks not to cast a thunder shroud
[02:55.22] Upon this place so full of joy
[03:00.18] A field of gold of loves employ
[03:06.16] So, why my heavy heart? you say
[04:48.04] When tears would stain the sights so gay
[04:53.50] My brother's dreams once here did soar
[04:59.22] Until he died at the hand of needless war
